From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:39:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: an A/B comparison of native Dolby Vision,
 as Hades sends it and as licensed players do

Licensed players send Dolby Vision TV-led in another form than Hades: no
active area (level 5), IPT, a neutral level 3 for content mapping v2.9,
level 254 at 0, BT.2020 in the AVI InfoFrame (a Homatics R 4K Plus, measured
by Hades; an OPPO UDP-203, fandangos/oppo-dv-mkv fix 24). Kodi of Hades has
settings for each (the form of the metadata of native Dolby Vision, expert
level). Which form looks right is a question of each TV: on an LG C1 and a
Hisense, fandangos measured that a positive lift of the trims (level 2) is
applied only where an active area is sent (CroqueMr/libreelec-CB1 #212),
and the TV's own player sends it. That data, TV by TV, is what settings
per TV need, and only a user with the TV in front of them can give it.

A new step of "Check this setup", "Dolby Vision: Hades or licensed players
(A/B)", not part of "Everything":
- it says what it compares and offers to copy the test clip
  (hades-check-ab-dv81.mkv of hades-check: a dark picture with black bars
  inside it, ten near-black squares, a ramp, trims with a lift and the
  level 5 of its bars) to a USB drive, to play it first with the TV's own
  player, the reference;
- it plays the clip twice, A and B, one as Hades sends it by default and
  one as licensed players send it, in an order chosen by chance (the
  answer is not the order's), each with its settings set for that play;
- it asks which looked right (A, B, the same, cannot tell, or both again)
  and whether the TV's own player was compared;
- the settings go back to what they were whatever happens: the journal of
  the check (restore.json, which hades-check-restore puts back into
  guisettings.xml before Kodi starts again where Kodi stopped in the
  middle) now holds these settings too, each of its type (an integer is
  written as a number);
- where a form was chosen and the settings are set otherwise, it offers
  to set them, naming every one; nothing changes without Yes;
- the answer is kept with the name of the TV from its EDID (manufacturer,
  product code and name; no serial number) in the summary of the check
  and in ab-results.json (the last 50), which the diagnostic report takes;
- where the clip did not go out as native Dolby Vision, nothing is
  offered and it says why to look at the picture of Dolby Vision 8.1.
A setting that this Kodi does not have is left out, and said in the result;
with none of them the step says it cannot run.

Strings 33800 to 33838, in English and the three Spanish ones.

Host tests (tools/regress/kodi-host/ux/check_ab_test.py, with stand-ins for
Kodi): the values of each form, the order, the offer, the journal of
integers and booleans and its return into guisettings.xml, the name of a
TV from its EDID, the file of the answers, and the whole flow: A and B
played with their settings, everything put back, Yes and No to the offer,
"the same", shown again, not native, the list closed, no such settings, the
copy to a drive. They fail without this patch.
